      object WelcomeTextMemo: TMemo
        Left = 0
        Height = 445
        Top = 25
        Width = 1192
        Align = alClient
        Lines.Strings = (
          'HTTP/JSON-over-POST interface code generator'
          'Prototype language: Pascal or C. Function/procedure declarations are'
          'auto-translated into LingoFuse HTTP POST + JSON interface code, so'
          'that webjs / PHP / nodejs and other languages without FFI can call'
          'Pascal / Python / C++ backends directly.'
          ''
          'Architecture: a 4-layer transparent conversion model'
          ''
          '  Layer 0   : original source (Pascal / C)'
          '              \_ unified via the "code modifier" model into:'
          '  Layer 1   : Pascal/C declaration body (text form, standard syntax)'
          '              <-> bi-directional conversion'
          '  Layer 2   : low-level structure (LV0)'
          '              \_ parsed by Z.Pascal_Func_Tool (Pascal) or Fill_C (C)'
          '              \_ exportable as LV0 JSON, editable externally to fix'
          '                 parse errors'
          '              |'
          '  Layer 3   : intermediate structure (LV1)'
          '              \_ built by TPascal_Func_Model with tnf_ABI normalization'
          '              \_ exportable as LV1 JSON, editable externally to adjust'
          '                 parameter descriptions, type mappings, etc.'
          '              |'
          '  Layer 4   : multi-target HTTP/JSON generators (7 independent units)'
          '              -- Pascal service -> <unit>_http_json_service_unit.pas'
          '              -- Pascal call    -> <unit>_http_json_call_unit.pas'
          '              -- Python service -> <unit>_http_json_service.py'
          '              -- Python call    -> <unit>_http_json_call.py'
          '              -- C++ service    -> <unit>_http_json_service.hpp / .cpp'
          '              -- C++ call       -> <unit>_http_json_call.hpp / .cpp'
          '              -- JavaScript call-> <unit>_http_json_call.js (+test html)'
          ''
          'Wire protocol (HTTP POST + JSON, UTF-8)'
          '  Inbound : webjs / PHP / nodejs'
          '            --HTTP POST--> bridge.py --LF_Call--> backend App'
          '  Outbound: backend App --LF_Call--> bridge.py --HTTP POST--> external'
          ''
          '  HTTP request : POST http://<bridge-host>:<port>/<app>/<api>'
          '  HTTP body    : UTF-8 encoded JSON'
          '  HTTP response: UTF-8 encoded JSON'
          '                 {"code": 0,  "result": ...}   success'
          '                 {"code": -1, "error": ...}    call failed'
          '                 {"code": -2, "error": ...}    bad request shape (HTTP 400)'
          '                 {"code": -3, "error": ...}    API not available'
          ''
          'Transparency notes'
          '- Every layer (LV0, LV1) has a JSON representation that can be'
          '  edited directly to fix metadata, without touching the original'
          '  source or re-parsing.'
          '- Edited JSON can be re-imported and drives the rest of the flow.'
          '- All target generators share the same LV1 structure:'
          '  "model once, emit many".'
          ''
          'Typical workflow'
          '1. Paste function declarations into the "Source code" editor'
          '   (Pascal or C syntax supported).'
          '2. Choose the source language (Pascal / C) or click "Auto-detect".'
          '3. Click "Parse -> JSON" to produce the LV0 low-level structure.'
          '4. Click "Next" to produce the LV1 intermediate structure.'
          '5. Click "Generate source" to emit the full artifact set:'
          '   - Pascal service + Pascal call'
          '   - Python service + Python call'
          '   - C++ service (.hpp + .cpp) + C++ call (.hpp + .cpp)'
          '   - JavaScript call (.js + test .html)'
          '   - Markdown README for every artifact family'
          '6. Build or run the generated files:'
          '   - Pascal service : lazbuild <unit>_http_json_service_unit.pas'
          '   - Python service : python <unit>_http_json_service.py'
          '   - C++ service    : g++ <unit>_http_json_service.cpp'
          '   - Every call side must first finish LingoFuse network setup'
          '     (LF_PrepareClient / LF_PrepareDone), then call the generated'
          '     free functions.'
          '7. webjs / PHP / nodejs can POST directly to bridge.py over HTTP;'
          '   no FFI required.'
          ''
          'Example deployment'
          '  Terminal 1 (Pascal beacon):'
          '      bridge_service.exe'
          ''
          '  Terminal 2 (Pascal worker node):'
          '      bridge_compute.exe'
          ''
          '  Terminal 3 (HTTP gateway):'
          '      python lingofuse\bridge.py --endpoint ipc:compute_grid --no-precheck --debug --port 8081'
          ''
          '  Terminal 4 (webjs / PHP / nodejs):'
          '      POST http://127.0.0.1:8081/pas/exp'
          '      Body: {"args": ["1+2*3"]}'
          ''
          'Future extensions'
          '- Add a "code modifier" for another language by translating its'
          '  declarations into a Pascal declaration body, and reuse every'
          '  downstream step.'
          '- Add new target generators (Rust / Go / Java / C# / ...) by'
          '  implementing the corresponding service and call generators.'
          '- LV0 / LV1 structures are stable and backward compatible.'
          ''
          'Getting started'
          '- "Source code" panel on the left: paste your code (Pascal / C).'
          '- Language selector at the top: pick manually or click the label'
          '  to auto-detect.'
          '- "Empty unit" button: insert a minimal skeleton template.'
          '- "Test unit" button: insert a complex example covering many'
          '  syntax variants.'
          '- Click "Generate source": artifacts appear under "Final source".'
          ''
          'If anything is unclear, consult the project documentation or the'
          'development team.'
          ''
          'Enjoy!'
        )
        ScrollBars = ssAutoVertical
        TabOrder = 1
        WordWrap = False
      end
    end
